    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are positioned for a high-ceiling offensive output today, anchored by **Yordan Alvarez** (82.97) and **Junior Caminero** (81.92). **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from a prime matchup against a struggling arm (xERA 5.48), with his elite .477 xwOBA creating a significant leverage opportunity in the two-hole. Similarly, **Junior Caminero** faces a favorable environment where park factors and SP weakness boost his projection, making him a must-start as he looks to capitalize on a +18% SP skill advantage. **Christian Yelich** also earns a strong recommendation (75.84); his matchup against Bubba Chandler is optimized by a +13% platoon boost and, crucially, a slow pitcher delivery that significantly elevates his stolen base potential\u2014a vital metric given our strategy of prioritizing speed in a tight 5x5 race.\n\nOur lineup construction emphasizes aggressive base-running and high-leverage spots, evidenced by the inclusion of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (62.22) and **Trea Turner** (67.32). While **Pete Crow-Armstrong** faces a minor platoon dip against a lefty, the 85% SB-rate environment created by the opposing battery ensures he remains in the lineup to hunt for steals. **Trea Turner** remains a cornerstone start despite facing a tougher southpaw, as his top-of-the-order positioning and dynamic platoon splits provide enough stability to weather the matchup. **Lars Nootbaar** (45.76) barely cleared the floor, as his projection suffered due to facing a formidable arm in Schlittler, but his platoon advantage keeps him marginally above the bench threshold.\n\nRegarding roster management, our bench is heavily impacted by off-days, with core assets like **Caleb Durbin**, **Colt Keith**, and **Carson Benge** all inactive. Consequently, the \"most interesting\" bench decision was simplified by attrition; with **Gary Sanchez** out of the starting lineup and no other viable bench depth available, our active starters are locked in by necessity rather than purely by marginal score calculation. We advise monitoring the status of **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Junior Caminero**, and **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, whose scores assume lineup stability; should any of these three drop in the order or be held out, the \"Lineup Pending\" variance could fluctuate their daily utility. We have sufficient depth in **Nelson Velazquez**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Josh Smith**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** should late-scratch alerts trigger a pivot.",
